  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 225 PM CDT Mon Aug 17 2026\n\nWednesday through Monday:\n\nSynopsis: The cold front responsible for Tuesdays storm potential is \nforecast to be south of the Wisconsin-Illinois border by Wednesday \nmorning, with drier northerly flow & passing high pressure leading \nto pleasant & precip-free conditions Wednesday afternoon through \nThursday. Winds will trend southwesterly on Friday, bringing milder \nand modestly more humid air to the region. The next cold front is \nforecast to move through the western Great Lakes Friday evening, \nwhen some scattered showers and thunderstorms will be possible. \nPleasant conditions will return by the Saturday-Sunday time frame \nbehind the departed front. High pressure will slide through the \nwestern Great Lakes Sunday into Monday, maintaining pleasant \nconditions through the conclusion of the long term period. \n\nFriday Afternoon-Evening: Appears that the next window for showers & \nthunderstorms will open along the next cold front. Similar to \nTuesdays setup, a combination of abundant synoptic forcing + \nsufficient wind shear points toward general favorability for more \norganized thunderstorms, with pre-frontal moisture return & \ninstability being the limiting factor on more precise storm \ncoverage, location, and intensity. Will be monitoring trends \nregarding these factors over coming forecasts & providing additional \nupdates as details clarify.\n\nQuigley",
